            "text": "{\"primary_meaning\":\"The presence, glory, and guidance of God (often referred to as the Shekinah glory), representing both His divine revelation and the veiling of His overwhelming majesty.\",\"primary_basis\":[\"Exodus 13:21-22\",\"Exodus 24:15-18\",\"1 Kings 8:10-11\",\"Matthew 17:5\"],\"alternatives\":[{\"meaning\":\"The vehicle or sign of Christ's return, divine authority, and judgment (apocalyptic clouds).\",\"basis\":[\"Daniel 7:13\",\"Matthew 24:30\",\"Revelation 1:7\",\"1 Thessalonians 4:17\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"A vast multitude or assembly of believers and saints.\",\"basis\":[\"Hebrews 12:1\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"Transience, the brevity of human life, or fleeting faithfulness.\",\"basis\":[\"Job 7:9\",\"Hosea 6:4\",\"Hosea 13:3\"],\"prominence\":\"minority\"},{\"meaning\":\"False teachers, disappointment, or empty promises (clouds without rain).\",\"basis\":[\"Jude 1:12\",\"Proverbs 25:14\"],\"prominence\":\"minority\"}],\"has_settled_consensus\":true,\"confidence\":\"high\",\"notes\":\"The cloud is one of the most prominent theophanic symbols in Scripture, primarily denoting God's manifest presence. Secondary meanings depend heavily on specific literary contexts, such as apocalyptic literature (Christ's return) or poetic metaphor (multitudes, transience, or falsehood).\"}",
